# Shopify MCP (GUISED)

This repo has two storefront surfaces:

- **Next.js Hygen site** — `app/`, `lib/`, `public/images/hygen/`
- **Shopify theme package** — `shopify-theme/` (Liquid sections/snippets matching the React homepage)

## Use Shopify Dev MCP

When working on Shopify docs, Liquid, GraphQL, or theme validation, use the `shopify-dev-mcp` tools instead of guessing APIs:

- `search_docs_chunks` — current Shopify documentation
- `learn_shopify_api` — API context before writing queries or theme code
- `validate_theme` — validate files under `shopify-theme/`
- `validate_theme_codeblocks` — validate Liquid snippets before suggesting them
- `validate_graphql_codeblocks` — validate Admin/Storefront GraphQL

## Keep surfaces aligned

When changing homepage content, navigation, collections, or product data:

1. Update the Next.js source (`app/components/`, `lib/products.ts`, `lib/site.ts`)
2. Mirror the same change in `shopify-theme/` when the Shopify theme should match
3. Use `shopify-theme/TRANSFER.md` for upload/merge steps

## Theme scope

`shopify-theme/` is homepage-focused. Commerce templates (product, cart, checkout) are out of scope unless explicitly requested.
